WEBVTT

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:03.140
Hello.

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:06.990
I'm Izumi Segawa, a first 
year at Hakuo Academy.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:09.200
I'm a class representative.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:13.150
If you like, please call me Class 
Representative Red: Red Izumi.

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:15.280
<b>Izumi Segawa</b>

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.120
And this is the class 
vice-representative, Blue,

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.950
and this is Black.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:24.350
The three of us together are 
Izumi Segawa and the other two.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:25.110
<b>And the Other Two</b>

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:27.360
Why are you treating us like that?!

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.270
And "the other two"?!

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:32.320
Well... that's what the cue card says.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:34.720
How could this be?

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:36.340
"The other two" is just mean!

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:41.270
Well, we always show up together, 
so why not introduce us as a group?

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:42.810
Yeah, but...

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:44.180
So on that note...

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:47.150
We're Izumi Segawa and the 
other two! Nice to meet you!

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:48.730
You're still using that?!

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:25.010
Hayata-kun, I've recently 
stumbled upon a secret.

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:26.480
A secret?

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:28.800
Yes, and a big one.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:29.870
I see...

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:31.580
You know Izumi and Miki, right?

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:33.420
Yes, they're always with you.

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:38.900
It's about them.

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:41.970
Please don't drink my milk.

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:44.560
The milk doesn't matter!

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:46.270
Do you even intend on listening?!

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:49.980
Why are you yelling at me?! 
Give me back my milk!

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:53.350
You don't have to get 
that angry over milk!

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:56.180
This is just a cute young 
girl playing around!

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:59.860
Okay, okay. So, what is the secret?

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:03.570
The three of us are 
always together, yes?

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:04.490
Yes.

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:08.140
We're often lumped together 
as a group because of that,

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:11.020
and recently, people have been 
calling us "the idiot trio."

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:14.500
I have the feeling people are
 lumping us together into one idiot.

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:18.880
<i>You didn't realize this until just now?</i>

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:20.280
I understand.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:21.900
Then, from now on, we'll take

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:24.330
care to call each of you 
an idiot individually.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:27.640
W-Wait! That's not the point!

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:30.140
I don't mind the three of us being a group!

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:33.770
I just don't like all three of us 
being seen as equally idiotic!

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:40.030
Because I'm smarter 
than those two idiots!

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:41.700
What?!

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:45.400
Well, it's true! 
I'm the smartest one of us!

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:47.950
What are you saying?! I'm smarter!

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:49.950
I'm not stupid either, you know!

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:51.520
You're both stupid!

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:52.330
<i>This is a pointless battle.</i>

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:52.960
Who are you calling stupid?! I'm not stupid!

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:55.620
Then why don't you all 
compare test scores

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:58.040
and decide who is the "King of Idiots"?

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:00.240
That's a bad idea!

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:03.170
Yeah! Test scores can't measure 
whether you're smart or not!

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:05.340
Let's not do that.

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:09.540
Then... how are you going 
to decide who's smartest?

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:10.770
I have a great idea.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:13.480
For what it's worth, we're all 
in the video research club.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:16.020
So we should have an 
interesting video showdown!

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:17.500
An interesting video...

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:18.490
...showdown?

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:22.390
Yes. We'll each film 
an interesting video

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:24.150
and upload it to a video site.

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:26.870
The number of views will decide the result!

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:29.230
One who is truly smart should be able to

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:31.700
film a video that will 
catch everyone's attention.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:33.030
I see.

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:34.540
That is a great idea!

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:37.330
Then, let's get started right away!

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:39.290
The one who gets the fewest
 views, the King of Idiots,

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:42.870
has to do a punishment game with 
Hayata-kun at the winner's command!

00:04:42.870 --> 00:04:43.780
All right!

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:47.660
Wait! What do you mean, 
a punishment game with me?!

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:48.760
Hey, come on!

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:52.050
It's okay. Don't worry, Hayata-kun.

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:57.060
Despite appearances, I'm confident 
that I can win first place.

00:04:57.600 --> 00:04:59.630
As thanks for always taking care of me,

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:02.440
I'll protect you, Hayata-kun!

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:04.520
Segawa-san...

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:07.760
I'd rather you thanked me 
some other way, though.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:10.030
Huh? Huh...?

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:14.370
So, what kind of video 
would be likely to win?

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:16.290
Well...

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:17.920
Ta-da!

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:19.670
A plant growth log!

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:22.540
That thing where I shoot 
a few frames each day,

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:23.920
and when played in sequence,

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:27.320
you can see the plant 
growing little by little!

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:29.680
I've actually been shooting 
it for a while already.

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:33.210
It'll grow big soon,

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:36.730
so when it's finished growing, 
I know it'll make an interesting video.

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:39.590
It's still a bit small, though.

00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:42.480
Y-Yeah, you're right...

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:46.490
It'd be nice if it would 
just shoot up for me...

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:53.440
Eek! I pulled it off!

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:56.590
What do I do, Hayata-kun?!
 What do I do?!

00:05:56.590 --> 00:05:59.300
You really are the 
King of Idiots, Izumi.

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:00.670
What?!

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:04.760
You two have no clue what videos 
need to become popular.

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:06.460
What videos need...

00:06:06.460 --> 00:06:08.330
...to become popular?

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:10.140
Yes. In short...

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:12.680
They need cute animals 
and deep emotion!

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:15.420
Listen.

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:18.400
There's no one in this world 
who wouldn't cry seeing

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:20.250
a movie where the animal dies after doing its best.

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:23.250
Well, that may be true, but...

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:24.800
And in the same way,

00:06:25.630 --> 00:06:27.820
there's something called 
"lovable animal moments"

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:30.320
that would make any human emotional.

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:32.400
Lovable moments?

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:35.600
Oh... But, Miki-chan, 
you don't have any pets.

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:37.180
I don't need to have any!

00:06:37.900 --> 00:06:40.460
Because some are about to be born now!

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:41.340
What?!

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:42.210
Born?

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:43.460
Behold!

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:45.820
I bought these eggs 
and incubated them at

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:47.560
95 degrees for three weeks.

00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:49.340
They'll hatch into chicks soon.

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:51.570
I'm going to spend lots 
of time filming them!

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:53.090
<i>Eggs that you...</i>

00:06:53.090 --> 00:06:54.160
<i>...bought?</i>

00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:58.910
Did you buy those eggs 
at the supermarket?

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:00.100
That's right.

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:02.050
And to ensure that they're born strong,

00:07:02.050 --> 00:07:04.820
I chose eggs from expensive 
Miyazaki free-range chickens.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:06.310
What? Then...

00:07:06.310 --> 00:07:09.450
Oh, right. You think it will 
take a long time, don't you?

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:11.070
Shows what you know.

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:15.690
Chicken eggs take exactly three 
weeks of incubation to hatch.

00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:17.220
And today is that day.

00:07:17.730 --> 00:07:20.120
So I know they'll be born today!

00:07:22.260 --> 00:07:25.580
But, supermarket eggs
 are unfertilized...

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:28.130
so even if you incubate 
them, they won't hatch.

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:32.910
What's unfertilized?

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:35.300
They're eggs laid without mating.

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:38.550
Since the chickens didn't 
mate, the eggs can't hatch.

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:40.530
They have to be fertilized to hatch.

00:07:40.530 --> 00:07:43.860
So these eggs that I've 
so carefully incubated...

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:45.490
They're just rotten eggs.

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:49.150
Just... rotten eggs?

00:07:52.100 --> 00:07:54.660
I never thought she'd know 
so little about it...

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:57.410
Even I knew that much.

00:07:57.690 --> 00:07:59.740
We're flying!

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:06.790
Don't throw rotten eggs at us!

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:12.290
Really... This is why you two are idiots.

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:13.050
Risa!

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:14.100
Listen well.

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:16.500
The standard of smart 
videos is none other

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:18.310
than the Rube Goldberg Machine!

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:20.810
Behold, my machine!

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:24.230
Wow, that actually looks genuine!

00:08:25.850 --> 00:08:27.950
I've been putting this together

00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:29.960
bit by bit while studying for my exams!

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:31.740
Just study for your exams!

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:34.570
All I have to do is press this switch,

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:37.440
and at the end, it launches balloons.

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:39.850
I'm going to set up the camera,

00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:41.910
so you can all just watch with envy!

00:08:47.870 --> 00:08:49.130
After...

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:52.990
After I was willing to get a 
failing grade to make this...

00:08:52.990 --> 00:08:54.380
D-Don't worry!

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:55.880
It'll work next time!

00:08:56.460 --> 00:08:59.850
It turned out none of us 
could shoot a decent video.

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:02.140
But...

00:09:02.740 --> 00:09:04.780
You all learned something today, right?

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:09.360
You're all equally idiotic.

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:11.640
Hey, yeah!

00:09:11.640 --> 00:09:13.290
All three of us...

00:09:13.290 --> 00:09:15.360
...are idiots after all!

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:17.820
Is that what you expect us to say?!

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:21.120
<b>Shonen Sunday</b>

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:24.490
Hayate, something smells.
 What happened?

00:09:25.070 --> 00:09:27.520
I was made a fool of.

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:31.270
Hey...

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:34.170
What's wrong? Are you bored?

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:37.950
No. I just remembered 
something important.

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:39.350
Something important?

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:46.350
<b>Supplementary classes in session!! 
Textbook pages 62-65 
There will be a test!! 
Memorize this stuff already, idiots!
Yukiji</b>

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:42.010
I was thinking, after 
what happened yesterday,

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:44.360
and on my birthday this year,

00:09:44.360 --> 00:09:46.350
and considering this 
episode's subtitle...

00:09:47.750 --> 00:09:49.610
People don't fuss over me.

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:51.020
Oh.

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:52.260
I see.

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:54.690
By the way, what happened
 on your birthday?

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:56.700
I'll never forget it.

00:09:58.230 --> 00:09:59.320
Asakaze-san,

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:01.620
happy birthday.

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:04.080
Oh! Thanks, Hayata-kun!

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:05.510
Well, then.

00:10:07.260 --> 00:10:08.580
Hold it, Hayata-kun!

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:09.880
Huh? What is it?

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:12.470
My present! Where's my present?!

00:10:12.470 --> 00:10:15.840
You gave presents to 
Hina and Izumi, didn't you?!

00:10:16.180 --> 00:10:18.200
Why don't I get one?!

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:20.970
Th-That was to express 
my gratitude to them.

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:24.350
Are you saying you have nothing 
to be grateful to me for?!

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:26.980
Actually, there are things I'd 
rather you apologized to me for...

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:28.470
What?!

00:10:28.470 --> 00:10:29.980
What do you mean, what?!

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:32.920
I said "what?!" because 
I want to know "what"!

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:34.910
You don't have any idea?!

00:10:34.910 --> 00:10:38.210
Of course not! 
I have nothing to apologize for!

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:42.370
I get it.

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:44.740
I did bring something, so here.

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:48.210
Well, then! Why didn't you 
do that in the first place?

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:50.000
Here.

00:10:51.030 --> 00:10:52.250
What is this?

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:54.130
A four-leaf clover.

00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:57.130
I found it this morning while I was 
cleaning, and thought it would suffice.

00:10:57.600 --> 00:11:00.890
I pressed it, so use it for a bookmark.

00:11:02.170 --> 00:11:02.890
Bye.

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:07.180
I won't accept it!

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:07.180
<b>Memorize this stuff already!</b>

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:10.480
I see. You're right, he definitely 
wasn't fussing over you.

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:13.910
You see?! He treats me totally 
differently than he does her!

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:18.860
Still, you probably shouldn't pester 
him for that any further, Risa.

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:20.430
What? Why?

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:24.550
What is it, Miki? 
Why are you being so quiet?

00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:26.830
Because the difference...

00:11:27.090 --> 00:11:28.580
The difference...

00:11:29.550 --> 00:11:32.580
...is probably a difference 
in popularity.

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:35.380
It's that different?

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:36.840
Yeah.

00:11:38.990 --> 00:11:40.510
Who are you calling?

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:44.930
The best person to ask about 
popularity is someone who's popular.

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:46.600
Hello?

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:47.930
Hey! Is that you, Hina?

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:50.550
There's something I need to ask you!

00:11:50.550 --> 00:11:52.770
How can I become popular?

00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:55.480
Wait, aren't you in your 
supplementary class now?

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:57.270
Stop playing around and study.

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:01.110
She scolded me...

00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:02.510
She sure did.

00:12:02.510 --> 00:12:04.010
Okay! Then I'll try the next one!

00:12:04.010 --> 00:12:05.530
Stop before they get mad at you too!

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:07.950
<b>Supplementary classes in session!! 
Textbook pages 62-65 
There will be a test!! 
Memorize this stuff already, idiots!</b>

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:07.950
Shouldn't you just study already?

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:10.200
Huh? How to become popular?

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:13.460
Yes! I thought you 
would know, Nagi-chan!

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:18.460
Well... Doesn't being a 
popular girl mean being cute?

00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:21.930
Oh! Th-Then, how can I be cute?

00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:25.200
I'm always reading romance 
manga in <i>Sunday</i> myself

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:27.240
to study up on cuteness.

00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:28.470
You study with <i>Sunday</i>?

00:12:29.110 --> 00:12:31.640
I think a girl's cutest moment...

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:34.900
might be when she's blushing.

00:12:32.920 --> 00:12:34.880
<b>Making Huge Waves!!!!!!! 
Color Centerfold</b>

00:12:32.920 --> 00:12:34.880
<b>The sweetest development 
the world has ever seen!</b>

00:12:32.920 --> 00:12:34.880
Hearts Aflutter! 
Kamchatka Inferno 120%

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:37.520
Of course! Blushing!

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:40.420
Hina and Izumi do get 
embarrassed and blush all the time!

00:12:40.420 --> 00:12:42.330
That must mean you 
lead a life of shame.

00:12:42.330 --> 00:12:43.400
What does that mean?!

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:47.280
So if I can just make it to the 
Gandhara known as blushing,

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:49.660
I can be cute and popular, right?

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:51.140
Thanks, Nagi-chan!

00:12:51.610 --> 00:12:54.500
So, have you all memorized 
the material yet?

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:56.750
Oh! You came at a great 
time, Hayata-kun!

00:12:57.060 --> 00:12:58.630
Wh-What's going on?

00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:06.640
<b>Supplementary classes in session!! 
Textbook pages 62-65 
There will be a test!! 
Memorize this stuff already, idiots!
Yukiji</b>

00:12:58.770 --> 00:13:00.320
I have a favor to ask!

00:13:00.320 --> 00:13:03.220
What's something so embarrassing, 
it would make you blush?

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:06.240
Huh? Something so embarrassing, 
it would make me blush?

00:13:07.020 --> 00:13:09.550
Maybe the time I was 
half-asleep in class

00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:12.890
and called the teacher "Mom"...

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:16.150
Do you have anything, Izumi?

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:17.370
What? Me?

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:19.140
I bet Izumi has lots of them.

00:13:19.140 --> 00:13:20.320
They ignored me...

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:24.470
In middle school, I was 
kind of half-asleep, too...

00:13:23.550 --> 00:13:25.470
<b>Be quiet in
 the classroom!!</b>

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:27.660
and I went to school in my 
pajamas, with a kid's backpack on.

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:29.490
That was embarrassing.

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:31.700
You really do live a life of shame.

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:33.050
Why a kid's backpack?

00:13:33.050 --> 00:13:34.490
No idea.

00:13:34.490 --> 00:13:36.820
Your life of shame has 
made me realize...

00:13:36.820 --> 00:13:38.750
Stop calling it a life of shame!

00:13:39.090 --> 00:13:43.090
I just came up with the absolute 
worst of all Izumi's shames!

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:44.510
Oh! What is it?!

00:13:44.510 --> 00:13:46.840
The unusually high frequency of 
her panties being visible!

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:48.460
Her panties?!

00:13:48.990 --> 00:13:50.600
What are you remembering?!

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:54.020
You're right. Her panties 
are visible all the time.

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:55.890
Damn that little bitch!

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:57.350
Who are you calling a bitch?!

00:13:57.770 --> 00:13:58.600
However!

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:01.730
Knowing this means I have no 
choice but to experiment.

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:03.340
Experiment? You can't mean...

00:14:03.340 --> 00:14:05.240
you're going to strip here?!

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:08.100
Yes. With Hayata-kun here, 
it's the perfect time.

00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:10.550
Wait! Are you stupid?!

00:14:10.550 --> 00:14:13.690
Girls who blush are seen 
as cute and popular.

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:16.090
I'll trust that theory.

00:14:16.090 --> 00:14:17.250
Now, Hayata-kun!

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:20.000
Lift Izumi's skirt all you like!

00:14:21.490 --> 00:14:24.400
Why does Hayata-kun 
have to lift my skirt?!

00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:26.470
Aren't you the one who wants 
to be popular, Risa-chin?!

00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:28.310
Yeah! What are you saying?!

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:29.380
What do you mean, what?

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:32.260
It's an experiment to see 
whether a blushing girl is cute!

00:14:32.710 --> 00:14:36.060
If I take mine off, I can't see 
how cute I look when I blush!

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:38.150
I see. That's true.

00:14:38.150 --> 00:14:41.520
So I'll have the panties-showing 
pro, Izumi, do it for me!

00:14:41.830 --> 00:14:42.860
Don't call me a pro!

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:46.270
Okay, Hayata-kun, lift that skirt!

00:14:46.620 --> 00:14:48.740
You really are an idiot, aren't you?

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:50.280
Th-That's right.

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:53.490
If the other option is having 
Hayata-kun lift it...

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:55.490
then I'll lift it myself.

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:07.840
Huh? What's wrong with you three?

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:11.010
Thank you, Izumi. 
So this is Gandhara...

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:13.170
I've seen the true talent of a pro.

00:15:13.170 --> 00:15:14.350
Huh? Huh?

00:15:14.990 --> 00:15:18.560
Now I understand why 
you're so cute and popular.

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:20.300
Uh, thanks?

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:22.480
Regardless,

00:15:22.790 --> 00:15:25.440
I'd like to get this 
supplementary test started.

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:26.480
Did you memorize everything?

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:27.430
No!

00:15:27.430 --> 00:15:28.400
Not yet!

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:29.650
Um...

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:31.780
I'm home.

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:35.230
Your face is red. What's wrong?

00:15:35.230 --> 00:15:36.080
Nothing...

00:15:36.610 --> 00:15:38.140
I was just thinking, a grade school kid

00:15:38.140 --> 00:15:40.390
who saw this would probably 
develop some weird fetish...

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:44.040
<b>Commercial Connecting Theater</b>

00:15:41.530 --> 00:15:42.600
I'll get you!

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:44.040
Catch me if you can!

00:15:44.350 --> 00:15:47.530
Why can't we study like Hina?

00:15:47.530 --> 00:15:49.240
It's unfair.

00:15:49.640 --> 00:15:51.560
Perhaps it's an issue of concentration?

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:56.740
No! Unlike you, we just 
have too many things to do!

00:15:56.740 --> 00:15:58.060
Such as?

00:15:58.060 --> 00:16:00.920
Like watching videos online of 
snakes swallowing sheep whole...

00:15:59.700 --> 00:16:01.620
<b>Baa~</b>

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:03.560
And watching videos of huge 
tigers raised by dogs!

00:16:01.790 --> 00:16:03.550
<b>Arf!</b>

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:08.930
<b>Student Council President</b>

00:16:06.100 --> 00:16:08.490
<i>Sounds like an issue with concentration to me...</i>

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:11.900
<b>Commercial Connecting Theater</b>

00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:11.900
Maybe I'll dye my hair pink...

00:16:12.180 --> 00:16:15.190
So this is the video of a snake 
swallowing a sheep whole?

00:16:15.190 --> 00:16:17.050
Nature really is something.

00:16:17.920 --> 00:16:21.910
Oh, this is the video of a 
huge tiger raised by a dog?

00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:22.870
It's cute!

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:24.380
<b>First Semester Midterm Exam</b>

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:24.380
<b>Hinagiku Katsura</b>

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:24.380
<b>Izumi Segawa</b>

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:24.380
<b>Miki</b>

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:24.380
<b>Risa Asakaze</b>

00:16:24.380 --> 00:16:25.750
Why?!

00:16:26.240 --> 00:16:29.000
I told you, it's a difference 
in concentration.

00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:32.010
Here, class rep. Hand these out.

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:35.060
I only printed one per
 student, so don't lose any.

00:16:36.290 --> 00:16:39.770
